{
  "_about": "Candidate SQL words of decision D153 and D158, from the engines' own keyword sources. The field matrix (stage k, cell place:key-sql-words-create|k) creates each word, from all four lists, as an unquoted column on the engine under test. MySQL: information_schema.KEYWORDS where RESERVED = 1 (MySQL 8.4.7). PostgreSQL: pg_get_keywords() where catcode is R or T (PostgreSQL 18.1). SQLite: the documented keyword list (SQLite 3.43.2 library words; the documented 147 words). MariaDB (D158): the candidate words of the MariaDB 13.0.2 reserved-word documentation, as typed from that list, each created as an unquoted column; the list holds those the server refuses (240 of 252). The candidates the server accepts are not in the list (ACCESSIBLE, DATABASE, GENERAL, IGNORE_SERVER_IDS, MASTER_HEARTBEAT_PERIOD, MASTER_SSL_VERIFY_SERVER_CERT, OPTION, POSITION, RANK, SCHEMA, SLOW, WINDOW are accepted by MariaDB 13.0.2; they are not added by the MariaDB source).",
